WEBVTT

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:20.783
Sorry!

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.721
Obviously, Ensign Baytart
doesn't appreciate music.

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:25.884
It's the darn fluid conduits
running through the walls.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.119
They conduct sound.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.923
You think when they designed
this thing, they would've...

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:31.726
The ship was built
for combat performance, Harry,

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:32.789
not musical performance.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:35.801
Nobody figured
we'd be taking any long trips.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.996
Where am I supposed to practice?

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.665
How about cargo bay?

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.606
Bad acoustics.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:44.439
We could get Baytart transferred
to the night shift.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.839
Couldn't do that.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:48.939
Could we?

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.014
So now you have an excuse
to give your mother

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.052
why you didn't practice
while you were gone.

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:59.992
Look, I'm trying to prepare
for an important performance.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.015
Oh, really?

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.389
Are we scheduled to rendezvous

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:04.329
with the Delta Quadrant
Symphony Orchestra?

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:07.561
No. Susan Nicoletti and I
have been working on

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.625
a new orchestral program
for the holodeck.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.967
Lieutenant Nicoletti?

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:14.974
The one I've been chasing
for six months?

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.474
Cold hands, cold heart?

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.739
Not when she plays the oboe.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:21.576
Chakotay to all senior officers.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.809
Please report to the Bridge.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.511
You know, Harry,

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:28.180
I've always wanted to learn
how to play the drums.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.698
I am picking up communication
satellites in orbit.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.202
They're nonfunctional.

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:46.228
Mr. Paris, take us
in a little closer.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:47.398
Mr. Kim, scan the surface.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:55.544
Captain, this used to be
a major trading spot.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:56.742
How long ago?

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.307
I'm not sure exactly.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.841
If I had to guess...

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:01.353
EM signature indicates

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:04.447
that a major solar flare
occurred here 19 years ago.

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:07.619
I'd say about 19 years...

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.627
more or less.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:11.152
Looks like a glacial freeze.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.186
Caused by a solar flare

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:14.200
that radically changed
the weather patterns.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.099
It did a lot more than that.

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:19.435
They were hit by magnetic storms
and extreme levels of radiation.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.372
Those glaciers are receding.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.875
The biosphere seems
to be recovering.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.741
Did anyone survive?

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.643
I'm scanning the settlement.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.511
There's evidence
of advanced technology...

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:31.881
warp reactors,
subspace transmitters...

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:34.182
but no life signs.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:37.553
Maybe they saw it coming
and evacuated the planet.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.956
Indications are that any attempt
at an evacuation

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:42.655
would have been prevented
by the atmospheric disturbances.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:45.664
What was
the estimated population?

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.962
Approximately 400,000.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:48.968
Captain.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:51.596
I'm picking up something
from the surface.

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.701
I think we're being hailed.

00:04:47.852 --> 00:04:50.150
I thought you said
there weren't any life signs.

00:04:50.187 --> 00:04:51.279
There aren't.

00:04:51.322 --> 00:04:53.790
I scanned the entire surface.

00:04:53.824 --> 00:04:56.292
Must be an automated signal.

00:04:56.327 --> 00:04:57.988
Let's hear it.

00:04:58.062 --> 00:05:02.396
I am Viorsa,
planner for the Kohl settlement.

00:05:02.433 --> 00:05:05.163
Your sensors have activated
this message.

00:05:05.202 --> 00:05:08.865
By now, you must be aware
of the catastrophic disaster

00:05:08.906 --> 00:05:11.033
that has destroyed our home.

00:05:11.075 --> 00:05:13.703
A few of us
have managed to survive

00:05:13.744 --> 00:05:16.372
in a state
of artificial hibernation,

00:05:16.414 --> 00:05:21.044
programmed to end in 15 years
from the date this was recorded.

00:05:21.085 --> 00:05:24.316
At that time,
when the eco recovery has begun,

00:05:24.355 --> 00:05:28.121
we will attempt
to rebuild our settlement.

00:05:28.159 --> 00:05:32.391
Please do nothing
to interrupt our timetable.

00:05:34.865 --> 00:05:36.594
Their timetable was supposed
to end four years ago.

00:05:36.634 --> 00:05:38.864
Looks like they didn't make it.

00:05:38.903 --> 00:05:42.270
Mr. Kim, wouldn't your scans
have picked up

00:05:42.306 --> 00:05:44.103
suppressed metabolic activity?

00:05:44.141 --> 00:05:45.802
I would think so, Captain.

00:05:45.843 --> 00:05:47.367
Unless...

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:51.247
Checking below the surface.

00:05:51.282 --> 00:05:53.750
Nothing one kilometer down.

00:05:53.784 --> 00:05:54.808
Two kilometers...

00:05:55.853 --> 00:05:57.320
Wait a minute.

00:05:57.354 --> 00:05:58.844
I think I've got something.

00:05:58.889 --> 00:06:02.757
2.3 kilometers down...
extremely faint bio-signatures.

00:06:02.793 --> 00:06:04.055
Three humanoids.

00:06:04.095 --> 00:06:06.359
Can you detect a malfunction
in their systems?

00:06:06.397 --> 00:06:09.093
Something to explain why they
didn't wake up on schedule?

00:06:09.133 --> 00:06:10.691
Not at this distance.

00:06:10.734 --> 00:06:12.929
But I am picking up
two more humanoids

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:14.961
at the same location
who are dead.

00:06:16.006 --> 00:06:18.099
Are there any
automated security systems?

00:06:18.142 --> 00:06:19.939
We triggered
a "do not disturb" sign.

00:06:19.977 --> 00:06:21.706
I don't want
to set off anything worse.

00:06:21.745 --> 00:06:23.542
No weapons of any kind, Captain.

00:06:23.581 --> 00:06:26.516
It is safe to transport
the hibernation pods to Voyager,

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:27.915
if that is your intent.

00:06:27.952 --> 00:06:28.919
It is.

00:06:28.953 --> 00:06:30.944
Prepare to beam them
to Cargo Bay 1.

00:06:31.055 --> 00:06:32.249
Mr. Kim, you're with me.

00:06:32.289 --> 00:06:34.189
Janeway to Kes,
report to Cargo Bay 1.

00:06:34.225 --> 00:06:35.419
Bring your medical gear.

00:06:35.459 --> 00:06:36.824
Aye, Captain.

00:06:47.104 --> 00:06:48.503
Two humanoids dead.

00:06:48.539 --> 00:06:50.507
Three humanoids in deep stasis.

00:06:54.745 --> 00:06:57.236
Life signs apparently stable.

00:07:00.518 --> 00:07:01.951
Our messenger.

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:14.561
Did the system break down?

00:07:15.633 --> 00:07:18.534
Not that I can see.

00:07:18.569 --> 00:07:20.537
I'm not reading
any pathway failures

00:07:20.571 --> 00:07:21.970
in the hibernation pods.

00:07:23.774 --> 00:07:26.334
The circuitry all seems
to be functioning.

00:07:31.348 --> 00:07:33.816
It looks like their brains
are interconnected

00:07:33.851 --> 00:07:37.844
in a complex sensory system
controlled by this computer.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.494
According to these indicators,
Captain,

00:07:44.528 --> 00:07:45.722
their minds are active.

00:07:45.763 --> 00:07:47.390
Active?
What do you mean?

00:07:47.431 --> 00:07:50.696
The encephalographic reading
suggests they're dreaming,

00:07:50.734 --> 00:07:53.498
but there's some kind of
interactivity with the computer.

00:07:53.537 --> 00:07:55.869
It's not just scanning
their brain functions.

00:07:55.906 --> 00:07:58.500
It's sending a data stream
back to them, as well.

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:01.534
Could it be generating

00:08:01.579 --> 00:08:04.275
an artificial environment
of some sort?

00:08:04.315 --> 00:08:06.249
Artificial environment?

00:08:06.283 --> 00:08:10.879
Years ago, Starfleet
used a technology

00:08:10.921 --> 00:08:14.914
to assist deep space travel
that kept the body in stasis,

00:08:14.959 --> 00:08:17.450
but provided a mental landscape

00:08:17.494 --> 00:08:19.928
to keep the mind
active and alert.

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:21.497
That sounds like
a pretty good way

00:08:21.532 --> 00:08:22.931
to wait out
a planetary disaster.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:26.299
For the moment,
it's as good a theory as any.

00:08:26.337 --> 00:08:28.168
So, what went wrong?

00:08:28.205 --> 00:08:30.571
Why are they still in there?

00:08:30.608 --> 00:08:31.939
The system was supposed

00:08:31.976 --> 00:08:33.944
to bring these people
out of hibernation

00:08:34.011 --> 00:08:35.603
four years ago.

00:08:35.646 --> 00:08:39.207
However, it wasn't left
entirely to the computer.

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:41.480
The programmers
obviously wanted

00:08:41.518 --> 00:08:43.645
the people in the system
to decide for themselves

00:08:43.687 --> 00:08:45.712
when it would be safe
to come out.

00:08:45.756 --> 00:08:47.621
This was accomplished
by a subroutine

00:08:47.658 --> 00:08:50.752
that periodically displayed
atmospheric conditions to them.

00:08:50.794 --> 00:08:51.920
So, they should've known
years ago

00:08:51.962 --> 00:08:53.088
that the biosphere
had recovered.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.461
Exactly.

00:08:54.498 --> 00:08:57.763
This subroutine has remained
available to these people

00:08:57.801 --> 00:09:00.099
since it was activated
four years ago.

00:09:00.137 --> 00:09:02.002
It's literally an escape hatch.

00:09:02.039 --> 00:09:03.472
Perhaps it has malfunctioned.

00:09:03.507 --> 00:09:06.908
No. That's what's so odd
about this.

00:09:07.011 --> 00:09:10.105
As far as I can tell,
it's working perfectly.

00:09:10.147 --> 00:09:11.842
Then why don't they
get themselves out?

00:09:11.882 --> 00:09:13.110
I don't know.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:14.310
Maybe they like it in there.

00:09:14.351 --> 00:09:15.909
I don't think so.

00:09:15.986 --> 00:09:17.248
Doctor?

00:09:17.288 --> 00:09:19.916
The two victims died
from massive heart failure

00:09:20.024 --> 00:09:22.754
and there was evidence
of prior neural trauma.

00:09:22.793 --> 00:09:24.784
I'm sorry.
What does that mean?

00:09:24.828 --> 00:09:28.264
It could be evidence
of extreme... fear.

00:09:28.299 --> 00:09:32.326
Maybe it was caused by the panic
that accompanies a heart attack.

00:09:32.369 --> 00:09:34.701
The readings suggest an extended
period of mental stress.

00:09:34.738 --> 00:09:36.729
Sounds like we ought
to get them out right away.

00:09:36.774 --> 00:09:38.537
Surely, Commander,
you're not suggesting

00:09:38.575 --> 00:09:40.566
we simply unplug them?

00:09:40.611 --> 00:09:42.169
Why not?

00:09:42.212 --> 00:09:44.339
Because you have three brains
whose survival

00:09:44.381 --> 00:09:47.111
has depended upon careful
monitoring by a sophisticated

00:09:47.151 --> 00:09:49.210
computer system for 19 years.

00:09:49.253 --> 00:09:50.515
The Doc is right.

00:09:50.554 --> 00:09:52.545
I have no idea
how to disconnect them

00:09:52.589 --> 00:09:54.284
without causing neural damage.

00:09:54.325 --> 00:09:57.089
I just don't know
the system well enough.

00:09:57.127 --> 00:09:58.719
They know the system.

00:09:58.762 --> 00:10:00.957
Why don't we ask them
how to proceed?

00:10:01.065 --> 00:10:02.862
How can we do that?

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:05.095
Lmplant a com-link
into their brains?

00:10:05.135 --> 00:10:07.296
We already have a means
of communication...

00:10:07.338 --> 00:10:08.737
the two unoccupied pods.

00:10:08.772 --> 00:10:12.799
We could add a backup
life support system,

00:10:12.843 --> 00:10:15.141
using our own computer
and medical stasis technology.

00:10:15.179 --> 00:10:17.477
The only way to help
those people is to go in

00:10:17.514 --> 00:10:19.379
and find out from them
what's wrong.

00:10:19.416 --> 00:10:21.407
I don't see any alternative.

00:10:24.054 --> 00:10:25.851
Neither do I.

00:10:25.923 --> 00:10:26.855
I'll be monitoring

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.414
your mental
and physical functions.

00:10:28.459 --> 00:10:31.690
If we detect
any unusual activity,

00:10:31.729 --> 00:10:33.788
you'll be transferred
onto our life support system

00:10:33.831 --> 00:10:35.321
and resuscitated.

00:10:35.366 --> 00:10:38.392
We've tapped into the system's
recall subroutine program.

00:10:38.435 --> 00:10:40.130
I'll give you five minutes
to look around,

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:41.296
then I'm bringing you back.

00:10:41.338 --> 00:10:42.999
Consider this a test run.

00:10:43.073 --> 00:10:44.233
Understood.

00:10:51.815 --> 00:10:53.908
Inducing primary stasis.

00:11:08.599 --> 00:11:11.261
Autonomic nervous system link
is secure.

00:11:11.301 --> 00:11:13.201
They're connecting
to the system.

00:11:15.606 --> 00:11:16.971
Looks like we made it.

00:11:17.074 --> 00:11:18.473
How do you feel?

00:11:21.311 --> 00:11:23.176
Normal.

00:11:46.134 --> 00:11:48.762
These must be characters
generated by the computer,

00:11:48.803 --> 00:11:50.794
but I don't see our people.

00:11:50.839 --> 00:11:52.238
Neither do I.

00:11:57.178 --> 00:11:59.169
Uh, excuse me.

00:12:01.783 --> 00:12:04.274
We're trying to find
some friends.

00:12:04.319 --> 00:12:06.446
Well, that shouldn't
be difficult.

00:12:07.922 --> 00:12:10.152
We're all friends here.

00:12:24.072 --> 00:12:26.836
- Oh, I'm sorry.
- Oh, I'm sorry.

00:12:26.875 --> 00:12:28.467
I didn't mean to bump into you.

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:29.602
You're new.

00:12:29.644 --> 00:12:31.839
Yes, we are.

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:33.814
Where are you from?

00:12:33.848 --> 00:12:35.213
Another town.

00:12:38.019 --> 00:12:40.044
There aren't any other towns.

00:12:43.925 --> 00:12:45.187
We're not getting very far.

00:12:47.295 --> 00:12:49.855
Perhaps I can help you.

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:54.325
You are looking for friends?

00:12:54.369 --> 00:12:55.996
That's right, three of them.

00:12:56.070 --> 00:12:58.971
And when you find
these friends?

00:12:59.007 --> 00:13:00.634
We want to talk to them.

00:13:00.675 --> 00:13:03.439
Why talk when we can dance?

00:13:25.066 --> 00:13:26.158
Let's get out of here.

00:13:26.201 --> 00:13:27.190
You got it.

00:13:29.237 --> 00:13:30.568
You!

00:13:37.479 --> 00:13:38.969
Take him.

00:13:39.013 --> 00:13:40.537
Harry.

00:13:43.651 --> 00:13:44.913
Harry!

00:13:49.691 --> 00:13:51.352
Harry!

00:13:57.298 --> 00:13:58.390
Harry!

00:14:13.113 --> 00:14:14.410
Stop!

00:14:16.383 --> 00:14:17.782
They're aliens!

00:14:17.818 --> 00:14:19.718
And they won't be alone.

00:14:19.753 --> 00:14:23.587
Kill them, and their shipmates
will shut down the program.

00:14:24.591 --> 00:14:25.580
Let him go!

00:14:27.661 --> 00:14:30.960
We knew this would happen
someday... that a ship

00:14:31.064 --> 00:14:32.326
would find us.

00:14:32.366 --> 00:14:34.391
It was only a matter of time.

00:14:34.434 --> 00:14:37.062
Only a matter of time, yes.

00:14:37.104 --> 00:14:39.766
Who knows what kind
of people they are?

00:14:39.806 --> 00:14:44.505
Who knows what will happen
to this world if you hurt them?

00:14:44.544 --> 00:14:46.171
I do.

00:14:46.213 --> 00:14:48.374
I know.

00:14:48.415 --> 00:14:49.973
Bring them here!

00:14:50.017 --> 00:14:52.349
Bring them here,
bring them here.

00:14:55.055 --> 00:14:56.454
You're like me.

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:58.185
A little of this
and a little of that.

00:15:01.661 --> 00:15:03.754
Ooh! My, what a temper.

00:15:03.797 --> 00:15:06.129
That's from your mother's side,
isn't it?

00:15:06.166 --> 00:15:09.067
Yes. You see?
I know everything.

00:15:09.102 --> 00:15:11.036
This is my world,

00:15:11.071 --> 00:15:12.504
my festival,

00:15:12.539 --> 00:15:14.530
and you're here
without an invitation.

00:15:14.574 --> 00:15:15.598
What is going on?

00:15:15.642 --> 00:15:16.700
Who is he?

00:15:16.743 --> 00:15:18.802
You will talk to me.

00:15:18.845 --> 00:15:20.472
I speak for them.

00:15:20.514 --> 00:15:22.607
And I speak for you, now.

00:15:22.649 --> 00:15:24.549
You don't understand that yet.

00:15:24.584 --> 00:15:26.279
You don't accept it...

00:15:26.319 --> 00:15:27.445
but you will.

00:15:27.487 --> 00:15:29.421
Are you a life-form

00:15:29.456 --> 00:15:33.222
or some kind of computer virus
that penetrated this system?

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:38.061
A virus, a virus

00:15:38.098 --> 00:15:39.725
He thinks I am a virus

00:15:39.766 --> 00:15:41.893
He thinks
I am a virus.

00:15:42.869 --> 00:15:44.700
Well, perhaps
I'll be a virus today.

00:15:46.073 --> 00:15:50.134
Oh, this one's got a mind
full of technical

00:15:50.177 --> 00:15:52.543
and operational
thoughts and ideas.

00:15:52.579 --> 00:15:54.570
Harry knows viruses.

00:15:54.614 --> 00:15:55.945
Stop this.

00:16:03.056 --> 00:16:07.254
I know you came here to get them
and take them away.

00:16:07.294 --> 00:16:10.354
But if you do that,

00:16:10.397 --> 00:16:12.024
we'll all disappear.

00:16:14.101 --> 00:16:16.262
Disappear.

00:16:16.303 --> 00:16:19.932
Because you're characters
created by this program.

00:16:19.973 --> 00:16:23.238
And once their minds stop
interacting with the system,

00:16:23.276 --> 00:16:25.403
you won't exist anymore.

00:16:25.445 --> 00:16:28.608
Ah, see the technical mind
at work.

00:16:28.648 --> 00:16:32.209
It seeks diagnostics,
data analysis.

00:16:32.252 --> 00:16:34.277
Well, here's some more data
for your mind

00:16:34.321 --> 00:16:35.879
to analyze and diagnose, Harry.

00:16:35.922 --> 00:16:38.618
Yes, I am merely
what has been created

00:16:38.658 --> 00:16:40.592
and is being created

00:16:40.627 --> 00:16:42.117
by his brain,

00:16:42.162 --> 00:16:47.498
his brain, her brain, and now...

00:16:47.534 --> 00:16:50.196
yours, and yours.

00:16:54.007 --> 00:16:54.996
Wha?

00:16:58.211 --> 00:17:00.008
What's this doing here now?

00:17:01.047 --> 00:17:02.071
This is your work.

00:17:02.115 --> 00:17:03.480
That's our wake-up call.

00:17:03.517 --> 00:17:06.816
It's been a real pleasure,
but... we're leaving.

00:17:06.853 --> 00:17:07.979
Come on.

00:17:09.789 --> 00:17:12.314
If you leave,
one of them will die.

00:17:12.359 --> 00:17:14.259
One of them will die.

00:17:14.294 --> 00:17:15.420
Try it and see.

00:17:15.462 --> 00:17:17.259
If you leave...

00:17:17.297 --> 00:17:18.264
he dies.

00:17:18.298 --> 00:17:19.424
He can do it.

00:17:19.466 --> 00:17:21.934
He's already killed
two of our colleagues.

00:17:22.035 --> 00:17:23.559
How is that possible?

00:17:23.603 --> 00:17:24.934
I cut off their heads.

00:17:25.038 --> 00:17:26.596
But none of this is real.

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:27.937
Of course it's real.

00:17:28.041 --> 00:17:29.599
As real as a nightmare.

00:17:29.643 --> 00:17:31.167
The two we found dead,

00:17:31.211 --> 00:17:33.771
both suffered
from massive heart attacks.

00:17:33.813 --> 00:17:35.337
Heart attack.

00:17:35.382 --> 00:17:38.180
Now, what might cause
a heart attack? Hmm.

00:17:38.218 --> 00:17:40.311
Unmanageable stress, perhaps?

00:17:40.353 --> 00:17:42.378
Unmanageable fear?

00:17:42.422 --> 00:17:44.652
The fear of losing a head,
perhaps?!

00:17:47.494 --> 00:17:49.587
You scared them to death.

00:17:55.735 --> 00:17:57.293
What's taking them so long?

00:17:57.337 --> 00:17:58.304
Life signs are stable.

00:17:58.338 --> 00:18:00.272
There's no interruption
in brain wave activity.

00:18:00.307 --> 00:18:02.275
The recall subroutine
is functioning.

00:18:02.309 --> 00:18:04.402
The window opened
for them on schedule.

00:18:04.444 --> 00:18:07.174
Captain, the norepinephrine
levels are rising.

00:18:07.214 --> 00:18:09.011
They're well above baseline.

00:18:09.049 --> 00:18:10.516
Some of that is to be expected,

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:12.575
but these levels indicate
abnormal stress.

00:18:12.619 --> 00:18:14.519
All right.

00:18:14.554 --> 00:18:16.852
I'm going to try to bring them
out with our backup systems.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:18.585
Initiating resuscitation.

00:18:22.762 --> 00:18:24.627
The body temperature is rising.

00:18:27.767 --> 00:18:29.291
What happened?

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:32.902
Their bodies are returning
to stasis condition, Captain.

00:18:32.939 --> 00:18:35.874
Someone is terminating
the recall command

00:18:35.909 --> 00:18:37.638
from inside the system.

00:18:41.715 --> 00:18:44.946
Very wise of you,
my technically minded fellow.

00:18:45.051 --> 00:18:46.484
Now, get rid of it completely.

00:18:46.519 --> 00:18:47.508
It's an intrusion.

00:18:47.554 --> 00:18:48.851
It's ruining the party.

00:18:48.888 --> 00:18:50.753
That would be a mistake.

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:53.054
No mistake.
A mistake if you refuse.

00:18:53.093 --> 00:18:54.822
You'd be missing an opportunity.

00:18:56.196 --> 00:18:57.322
Trying to get the better of me?

00:18:57.364 --> 00:18:59.127
Trying to trick me?

00:18:59.165 --> 00:19:01.633
I know everything you know,
Harry Kim.

00:19:01.668 --> 00:19:03.397
I know how much you miss Libby.

00:19:03.436 --> 00:19:05.427
I know how you can never hit
that G-sharp

00:19:05.472 --> 00:19:07.030
in the Mozart concerto.

00:19:07.073 --> 00:19:09.769
Do you think I don't know
you're trying to defeat me?

00:19:09.809 --> 00:19:12.539
Fine. So you know.

00:19:12.579 --> 00:19:15.844
You'll also know that what I'm
about to tell you is the truth.

00:19:15.882 --> 00:19:18.282
You'd be smart
to let one of us go.

00:19:18.318 --> 00:19:19.910
Would I?

00:19:19.986 --> 00:19:22.716
This is your chance to send
the outside world a message...

00:19:22.756 --> 00:19:24.690
to tell them your demands.

00:19:24.724 --> 00:19:26.487
I have only one demand...

00:19:26.526 --> 00:19:27.788
to exist.

00:19:27.827 --> 00:19:30.193
Then you'd better let us
tell them.

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:31.197
Otherwise, you run the risk

00:19:31.231 --> 00:19:32.755
of our people
shutting down the whole system,

00:19:32.799 --> 00:19:34.096
because I promise you,

00:19:34.134 --> 00:19:36.568
they won't let us stay
in here for long.

00:19:44.878 --> 00:19:47.244
How did this happen?

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:49.510
The system was designed
to be adaptive,

00:19:49.549 --> 00:19:51.710
to observe and respond
to our thoughts

00:19:51.751 --> 00:19:54.151
and adjust the environment
to our wishes.

00:19:55.155 --> 00:19:56.383
Who wished him up?

00:19:56.423 --> 00:19:59.392
It happened over months
without our even realizing it.

00:19:59.426 --> 00:20:01.860
All of us had fears
about survival, recovery.

00:20:01.895 --> 00:20:02.953
We never anticipated

00:20:03.029 --> 00:20:05.293
the computer would manifest
those fears into him.

00:20:05.332 --> 00:20:07.266
Our only hope was
that someone like you

00:20:07.300 --> 00:20:08.790
would come along and find us.

00:20:08.835 --> 00:20:11.303
It's almost as though
he can read our minds.

00:20:11.338 --> 00:20:12.965
He seems to know
what we're thinking.

00:20:13.006 --> 00:20:14.598
He's generated by the system,

00:20:14.641 --> 00:20:16.836
and our brains are monitored
by the system,

00:20:16.876 --> 00:20:18.969
so, yes, in a manner
of speaking, he can.

00:20:19.012 --> 00:20:20.639
But there is a delay

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:23.911
before he becomes aware
of what we're thinking.

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:26.510
It takes a few minutes
for our brain activity

00:20:26.553 --> 00:20:28.885
to be processed by the system.

00:20:28.922 --> 00:20:32.414
Well, I've come to a decision,
with the help of my friends.

00:20:32.459 --> 00:20:35.519
You, leave. You, stay.

00:20:35.562 --> 00:20:37.496
And tell your beloved
Captain Janeway

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:39.623
that if we die, they die,

00:20:39.666 --> 00:20:41.998
including you, dear Harry...

00:20:42.102 --> 00:20:44.570
you who becomes my best friend
as of today.

00:20:44.604 --> 00:20:47.300
Because she would never
kill you, would she, Harry?

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:51.276
No. Why, she's like a dear
old mother to you, isn't she?

00:20:51.311 --> 00:20:52.300
Go!

00:20:59.419 --> 00:21:01.649
Someone's activated
the recall subroutine.

00:21:01.688 --> 00:21:03.315
Captain, it's Lieutenant Torres.

00:21:07.293 --> 00:21:08.783
Her body temperature is rising.

00:21:08.828 --> 00:21:11.729
She should regain consciousness
in about... 12 minutes.

00:21:12.766 --> 00:21:14.757
At least, we'll finally
get the answers

00:21:14.801 --> 00:21:15.859
to a few questions.

00:21:25.477 --> 00:21:28.446
Well, let's start
with the obvious question.

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:31.449
If they're demanding to exist,

00:21:31.483 --> 00:21:33.917
can we find a way
to let them exist

00:21:33.952 --> 00:21:36.682
in this artificial world
of theirs?

00:21:36.721 --> 00:21:38.154
Not unless you're prepared

00:21:38.189 --> 00:21:40.521
to leave one person
in stasis permanently.

00:21:40.558 --> 00:21:42.753
I concur with Lieutenant Torres.

00:21:42.794 --> 00:21:44.557
The computer uses
bioneural feedback

00:21:44.596 --> 00:21:47.429
from the participants' brains
to create the environment.

00:21:47.465 --> 00:21:49.990
Doctor, is there a way
to speed up resuscitation?

00:21:50.101 --> 00:21:52.569
Only by a few minutes.

00:21:52.604 --> 00:21:55.004
Anything more, we'd be risking
serious brain damage.

00:21:55.106 --> 00:21:57.870
Ten minutes would be
about the best we could do.

00:21:57.909 --> 00:22:00.707
Ten minutes and all
the hostages could be killed.

00:22:00.745 --> 00:22:03.236
Then it seems to me
our first order of business

00:22:03.281 --> 00:22:05.613
should be to reduce
the number of hostages.

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:12.249
All we have to do now is decide
how to negotiate with...

00:22:12.290 --> 00:22:14.485
an emotion.

00:22:15.994 --> 00:22:18.895
With a manifestation...

00:22:18.930 --> 00:22:20.955
of fear.

00:22:20.999 --> 00:22:24.491
Fear is the most primitive,
the most primordial

00:22:24.536 --> 00:22:25.969
of biological responses.

00:22:26.071 --> 00:22:29.165
The ability
to recognize danger...

00:22:29.207 --> 00:22:30.538
to fight it or run away from it.

00:22:30.575 --> 00:22:31.667
That's what fear gives us,

00:22:31.709 --> 00:22:36.612
but... when fear
holds you hostage...

00:22:40.952 --> 00:22:43.819
how do you make it let go?

00:22:43.855 --> 00:22:46.153
Maybe we should try
to make them laugh.

00:22:46.191 --> 00:22:47.658
A good joke just...

00:22:49.327 --> 00:22:52.194
uh, seems to make fear dissolve.

00:22:52.230 --> 00:22:54.858
Well, it does in me, anyway.

00:22:54.899 --> 00:22:55.991
I think something

00:22:56.101 --> 00:22:59.366
a little more responsive
to The Clown's demand.

00:22:59.404 --> 00:23:02.430
B'Elanna, maybe you can come up

00:23:02.474 --> 00:23:05.443
with a way to modify the system

00:23:05.477 --> 00:23:08.605
so it can run
without bioneural interaction.

00:23:08.646 --> 00:23:09.908
How do we negotiate

00:23:09.948 --> 00:23:12.246
without sending in
another hostage?

00:23:12.283 --> 00:23:14.410
Good question.

00:23:14.452 --> 00:23:18.946
We have to come up with
a safer method of communication.

00:23:19.023 --> 00:23:21.787
I regret very much
what has happened to you.

00:23:21.826 --> 00:23:24.351
You came to help.

00:23:24.395 --> 00:23:26.226
You didn't deserve this.

00:23:29.901 --> 00:23:33.701
I regret so many things.

00:23:41.913 --> 00:23:43.073
Look.

00:23:44.082 --> 00:23:46.710
We don't have time for regret.

00:23:46.751 --> 00:23:49.584
My people are working
on a way... right now...

00:23:49.621 --> 00:23:50.986
to get us out of here,

00:23:51.055 --> 00:23:52.920
and we have to help
them if we can.

00:23:52.957 --> 00:23:57.257
You'll leave hope behind
after a few months of this.

00:24:02.700 --> 00:24:04.895
Why does he do it?

00:24:04.936 --> 00:24:08.167
We're his canvas...

00:24:08.206 --> 00:24:10.299
his blocks of marble.

00:24:10.341 --> 00:24:14.573
With us, he practices
his ghastly art.

00:24:14.612 --> 00:24:16.409
Thinking about escape,
are we, Harry?

00:24:16.447 --> 00:24:18.938
Naughty, naughty.

00:24:18.983 --> 00:24:20.951
I don't like those thoughts.

00:24:21.052 --> 00:24:23.612
We're going to have to do
something about them.

00:24:23.655 --> 00:24:24.679
He's new.

00:24:24.722 --> 00:24:26.485
He can't help thinking
about getting out.

00:24:26.524 --> 00:24:27.718
He can!

00:24:27.759 --> 00:24:29.522
You don't think about it
anymore.

00:24:29.561 --> 00:24:31.927
Oh, but he's new...

00:24:31.963 --> 00:24:33.521
and you're old.

00:24:33.565 --> 00:24:35.499
New and old...

00:24:35.533 --> 00:24:37.558
old and new.

00:24:37.602 --> 00:24:40.503
Well, then, the answer
is to simply...

00:24:40.538 --> 00:24:42.597
make you old, Harry.

00:24:44.676 --> 00:24:47.873
Are you afraid of growing old,
Harry?

00:24:47.912 --> 00:24:50.437
Is that what you fear...

00:24:50.481 --> 00:24:53.177
being cared for by nurses?

00:24:53.218 --> 00:24:55.880
Time for your medicine.

00:24:58.223 --> 00:25:01.386
You don't like being helpless,
do you, Harry?

00:25:01.426 --> 00:25:04.918
You like to take care
of yourself.

00:25:04.996 --> 00:25:07.464
Yes, I know how you hate

00:25:07.498 --> 00:25:09.932
to feel
like the baby on the crew.

00:25:15.573 --> 00:25:16.904
Ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

00:25:16.941 --> 00:25:18.932
Oh, what's the matter, Harry?

00:25:19.010 --> 00:25:22.571
Ooh, does my costume
frighten you, huh? Ooh!

00:25:22.614 --> 00:25:23.581
Coochie-coo.

00:25:25.550 --> 00:25:27.609
Yeah. Oh, look
at little Harry fly!

00:25:27.652 --> 00:25:28.744
Whoo!

00:25:28.786 --> 00:25:30.481
Whoo! There he goes!

00:25:30.521 --> 00:25:31.954
Whoo!

00:25:32.056 --> 00:25:33.921
Whee!

00:25:33.958 --> 00:25:35.220
All right, that's enough.

00:25:47.372 --> 00:25:51.274
This is not reality.

00:25:51.309 --> 00:25:52.799
It's an illusion.

00:25:52.844 --> 00:25:55.244
When your only reality
is an illusion,

00:25:55.280 --> 00:25:57.077
then illusion is a reality.

00:25:59.917 --> 00:26:01.578
Like the man said:

00:26:01.619 --> 00:26:06.921
"The only thing we have
to fear is fear itself."

00:26:06.991 --> 00:26:10.085
Oh, I thought we were
going to be friends.

00:26:10.128 --> 00:26:12.426
Didn't want to do this, Harry.

00:26:12.463 --> 00:26:14.931
No, I didn't want to bring this
up in front of the others,

00:26:15.033 --> 00:26:17.661
but I know
what really scares you.

00:26:17.702 --> 00:26:19.795
I know when you were nine

00:26:19.837 --> 00:26:21.930
and your parents took
you to that colony...

00:26:21.973 --> 00:26:23.668
the radiation disaster?

00:26:23.708 --> 00:26:25.699
Humanitarian mission?

00:26:25.743 --> 00:26:27.608
You visited a hospital!

00:26:27.645 --> 00:26:29.044
You remember.

00:26:30.782 --> 00:26:31.749
No.

00:26:31.783 --> 00:26:33.512
You wandered off by yourself

00:26:33.551 --> 00:26:36.213
where you weren't
supposed to be.

00:26:36.254 --> 00:26:38.313
The only thing we have to fear
is fear itself.

00:26:38.356 --> 00:26:42.690
You saw people and things
you weren't supposed to see...

00:26:42.727 --> 00:26:44.592
sick and dying...

00:26:44.629 --> 00:26:45.926
Keep repeating:

00:26:45.963 --> 00:26:47.658
"The only thing we have to fear

00:26:47.699 --> 00:26:48.825
is fear itself!"

00:26:48.866 --> 00:26:51.835
"The only thing we have to fear
is fear itself."

00:26:51.869 --> 00:26:53.769
And how about:
"There's no place like home!

00:26:53.805 --> 00:26:55.636
There's no place like home!"

00:26:57.108 --> 00:26:59.406
Try clicking your heels
together three times.

00:26:59.444 --> 00:27:02.311
Oh, but your legs
are restrained, aren't they?

00:27:02.347 --> 00:27:05.475
Just like that little girl
you saw on the operating table?

00:27:05.516 --> 00:27:08.781
The doctor called
for a scalpel...

00:27:09.954 --> 00:27:11.546
She looked at you,

00:27:11.589 --> 00:27:14.524
her face filled with fear.

00:27:15.560 --> 00:27:18.586
Fear... fear.

00:27:18.629 --> 00:27:20.688
Fear.

00:27:20.732 --> 00:27:22.757
Do you remember?!

00:27:22.800 --> 00:27:25.428
No!

00:27:25.470 --> 00:27:26.937
Excuse me.

00:27:27.038 --> 00:27:28.938
You're not holding that
properly.

00:27:29.040 --> 00:27:30.837
Correct positioning
of the index finger

00:27:30.875 --> 00:27:32.570
is necessary
for optimal dexterity.

00:27:34.579 --> 00:27:35.568
Who are you?!

00:27:35.613 --> 00:27:38.309
I'm Captain Janeway's
representative.

00:27:38.349 --> 00:27:40.544
I'm here to negotiate with you.

00:27:40.585 --> 00:27:42.610
Are you well, Mr. Kim?

00:27:42.653 --> 00:27:44.883
I'm starting to feel better.

00:27:44.922 --> 00:27:46.355
You're different.

00:27:46.391 --> 00:27:48.621
I don't know anything about you.

00:27:48.659 --> 00:27:49.785
You're not on the system.

00:27:49.827 --> 00:27:52.057
I would be pleased to tell you
all about myself

00:27:52.096 --> 00:27:53.393
at a more appropriate time.

00:27:53.431 --> 00:27:54.762
For now, suffice it to say

00:27:54.799 --> 00:27:56.926
that I am here
by a miracle of technology.

00:27:56.968 --> 00:27:59.368
Now, let's get down
to the issues, shall we?

00:27:59.404 --> 00:28:00.962
How am I supposed to negotiate

00:28:01.038 --> 00:28:02.903
if I don't know
what you're thinking?

00:28:03.007 --> 00:28:05.066
I have a very trustworthy face.

00:28:05.109 --> 00:28:06.872
My Captain is prepared

00:28:06.911 --> 00:28:08.811
to give you exactly
what you ask for

00:28:08.846 --> 00:28:11.371
under the condition you release
all the hostages.

00:28:12.650 --> 00:28:13.912
Release the hostages?!

00:28:13.951 --> 00:28:16.784
We would provide continuing
input from a simulated brain.

00:28:16.821 --> 00:28:18.755
A computer model
that would generate...

00:28:18.790 --> 00:28:20.815
Simulated brain? Simulated?

00:28:20.858 --> 00:28:21.916
I myself have a com...

00:28:21.959 --> 00:28:22.926
It won't work.

00:28:22.960 --> 00:28:24.655
It's a lie. Tell 'em, Harry.

00:28:24.695 --> 00:28:26.458
I don't know that for sure.

00:28:26.497 --> 00:28:27.464
Liar!

00:28:27.498 --> 00:28:28.465
Viorsa!

00:28:28.499 --> 00:28:29.796
Get over here.

00:28:31.602 --> 00:28:32.569
Tell him.

00:28:32.603 --> 00:28:36.266
It might require a recalibration
of the optronic pathways...

00:28:36.307 --> 00:28:37.865
Liar! After all this time,

00:28:37.909 --> 00:28:40.309
do you think I can't tell
when you lie?!

00:28:42.747 --> 00:28:44.271
- The simulated brain...
- Would leave me

00:28:44.315 --> 00:28:45.304
at your mercy!

00:28:45.349 --> 00:28:48.284
No. They stay.

00:28:48.319 --> 00:28:50.287
The Captain is prepared
to risk the lives

00:28:50.321 --> 00:28:52.152
of the hostages
rather than leave them

00:28:52.190 --> 00:28:53.418
under your control.

00:28:53.458 --> 00:28:55.892
Who is she to tell me
what I have to do?

00:28:55.927 --> 00:28:59.226
She's the one out there with
the "off" switch in her hand.

00:28:59.263 --> 00:29:01.128
She would never kill Harry.

00:29:01.165 --> 00:29:04.157
I'd rather die than spend
my life in here with you.

00:29:04.202 --> 00:29:06.466
She knows that.

00:29:06.504 --> 00:29:08.062
I won't let them go.

00:29:08.105 --> 00:29:09.697
A compromise.

00:29:09.740 --> 00:29:11.071
Let some of them go.

00:29:11.108 --> 00:29:12.268
No.

00:29:12.310 --> 00:29:13.834
We've studied your system.

00:29:13.878 --> 00:29:15.368
You only need one to survive.

00:29:15.413 --> 00:29:17.677
And if that one gets sick
and dies?

00:29:17.715 --> 00:29:19.307
No! I need them all.

00:29:19.350 --> 00:29:20.578
Now go away

00:29:20.618 --> 00:29:23.348
and tell your Captain Janeway
I'm disappointed.

00:29:23.387 --> 00:29:24.854
I expected more from her.

00:29:24.889 --> 00:29:26.151
If we could just...

00:29:26.190 --> 00:29:27.418
Go away!

00:29:27.458 --> 00:29:28.789
Go away! Go away!

00:29:32.263 --> 00:29:33.230
I'll be back.

00:29:33.264 --> 00:29:34.458
Go away!

00:29:34.499 --> 00:29:40.563
Go away! Go away! Go away!

00:29:40.638 --> 00:29:43.801
Well, I'm sorry I don't live up
to his expectations.

00:29:43.841 --> 00:29:45.570
What's your opinion of him,
Doctor?

00:29:45.610 --> 00:29:47.043
Unstable...

00:29:47.078 --> 00:29:48.306
unpredictable.

00:29:48.346 --> 00:29:49.870
Everything you'd
expect from "fear."

00:29:49.914 --> 00:29:52.439
Captain, the longer
we allow this to continue,

00:29:52.483 --> 00:29:53.677
the more likely it is that he

00:29:53.718 --> 00:29:55.709
will take his frustrations
out on the hostages.

00:29:55.753 --> 00:29:57.345
I agree.

00:29:57.388 --> 00:29:59.322
And I can't allow that
to happen.

00:29:59.357 --> 00:30:02.793
We're going to have to mount
some kind of rescue mission.

00:30:09.232 --> 00:30:12.258
Doctor, if we do simply
disconnect the hostages...

00:30:12.302 --> 00:30:14.133
There would certainly
be brain damage.

00:30:14.170 --> 00:30:15.501
How much damage?

00:30:15.538 --> 00:30:16.835
Could you possibly repair it?

00:30:16.873 --> 00:30:18.238
Possibly? Yes.

00:30:18.274 --> 00:30:19.639
Would Mr. Kim still be able

00:30:19.676 --> 00:30:21.541
to hold his clarinet
when I was done?

00:30:21.578 --> 00:30:22.545
Possibly.

00:30:22.579 --> 00:30:24.979
The brain is such
an interesting organ.

00:30:25.048 --> 00:30:26.913
Could we switch over
to a simulated brain

00:30:26.950 --> 00:30:28.315
without The Clown noticing it?

00:30:28.351 --> 00:30:29.818
Oh, he'd notice.

00:30:29.853 --> 00:30:31.184
He was very smart to reject

00:30:31.221 --> 00:30:33.121
the whole notion
of a simulated brain.

00:30:33.156 --> 00:30:34.418
It just wouldn't be the same.

00:30:34.457 --> 00:30:36.652
There is no way
an artificial intelligence

00:30:36.693 --> 00:30:39.093
can replace
actual brain functions.

00:30:39.129 --> 00:30:41.825
I'll choose not to take
that personally, Lieutenant.

00:30:41.865 --> 00:30:44.629
For what it's worth, Mr. Viorsa
suggested there would be a way

00:30:44.667 --> 00:30:47.329
to make a simulated brain
function in this system.

00:30:47.370 --> 00:30:49.804
He suggested it would take...

00:30:49.839 --> 00:30:53.036
a "recalibration
of the optronic pathways."

00:30:54.844 --> 00:30:56.607
I don't know what he could
have been talking about.

00:30:56.646 --> 00:30:57.670
The optronic pathways

00:30:57.714 --> 00:30:59.841
have nothing to do
with the neural interface.

00:30:59.883 --> 00:31:02.215
It doesn't make any sense.

00:31:02.252 --> 00:31:05.050
Then, perhaps he had
another reason for saying it.

00:31:05.088 --> 00:31:07.215
How do the optronic
pathways function

00:31:07.257 --> 00:31:08.747
in this system, B'Elanna?

00:31:08.792 --> 00:31:09.952
They... they control

00:31:10.060 --> 00:31:12.426
the basic elements
of the environment,

00:31:12.462 --> 00:31:14.589
access data banks
that were programmed

00:31:14.631 --> 00:31:16.258
when the system was created.

00:31:20.036 --> 00:31:23.062
If we interrupt
the optronic pathways,

00:31:23.106 --> 00:31:26.507
we could disassemble
that entire world

00:31:26.543 --> 00:31:29.671
and its characters,
piece by piece.

00:31:29.712 --> 00:31:34.081
If we can't remove the hostages
from the environment,

00:31:34.117 --> 00:31:36.813
then we might be able
to remove the environment

00:31:36.853 --> 00:31:39.287
from the hostages.

00:31:39.322 --> 00:31:41.153
How did Viorsa manage
to communicate this

00:31:41.191 --> 00:31:42.783
without The Clown
knowing about it?

00:31:42.826 --> 00:31:45.761
Perhaps it was because The
Clown's attention was divided

00:31:45.795 --> 00:31:46.955
at the time.

00:31:46.996 --> 00:31:48.327
And you're going to continue

00:31:48.364 --> 00:31:50.423
to provide him
with distractions, Doctor.

00:31:50.467 --> 00:31:53.368
B'Elanna, how long will it take
to block these pathways?

00:31:53.403 --> 00:31:55.769
I'm not sure how many there are,
Captain.

00:31:55.805 --> 00:31:56.965
And I'll have to do it manually,

00:31:57.006 --> 00:31:58.837
because we don't know
how to deprogram the system.

00:31:58.875 --> 00:32:01.002
You'll only have
a few minutes at best.

00:32:01.077 --> 00:32:03.568
Once "fear" knows
what we're up to,

00:32:03.613 --> 00:32:05.342
it'll be a race against time

00:32:05.381 --> 00:32:07.645
to save the lives
of those hostages.

00:32:07.684 --> 00:32:09.515
Bravo! Bravo!

00:32:09.552 --> 00:32:10.541
Go away!

00:32:10.587 --> 00:32:11.952
I want to be alone.

00:32:11.988 --> 00:32:13.853
You're ruining the festival.

00:32:13.890 --> 00:32:16.085
Don't be a poop!

00:32:16.126 --> 00:32:17.559
I can't help it.

00:32:17.594 --> 00:32:19.084
I'm feeling sorry for myself.

00:32:19.129 --> 00:32:21.290
Well, don't take it out on us.

00:32:21.331 --> 00:32:23.094
Take it out on them.

00:32:24.934 --> 00:32:26.492
You people...

00:32:26.536 --> 00:32:28.367
you wonderful people...

00:32:28.404 --> 00:32:29.530
my friends...

00:32:30.607 --> 00:32:33.132
You do know how to make a man
feel better, don't you?

00:32:33.176 --> 00:32:36.168
Okay, then, what shall we play?

00:32:36.212 --> 00:32:38.646
The insect game.

00:32:38.681 --> 00:32:40.046
Yes, yes.
The insect game.

00:32:43.953 --> 00:32:45.079
You again?

00:32:45.121 --> 00:32:47.248
You're the one
who ruined my mood.

00:32:47.290 --> 00:32:49.258
You and your sweet Captain.

00:32:49.292 --> 00:32:52.193
My sweet Captain
has a new offer to make.

00:32:52.228 --> 00:32:53.889
No simulated brains.

00:32:53.930 --> 00:32:54.988
I want real brains.

00:32:55.031 --> 00:32:55.998
The Captain is prepared

00:32:56.099 --> 00:32:58.624
to give you...
a cloaking device.

00:32:58.668 --> 00:33:00.329
I already have
a cloaking device.

00:33:00.370 --> 00:33:02.668
Thank you anyway.

00:33:02.705 --> 00:33:04.468
I'm talking about a device
that would shield you

00:33:04.507 --> 00:33:08.136
from being detected by any
other interstellar visitors.

00:33:19.389 --> 00:33:22.290
There are almost 40 pathways
to disable, Captain,

00:33:22.325 --> 00:33:23.758
but I should be able
to get it done

00:33:23.793 --> 00:33:25.090
in under two minutes.

00:33:25.128 --> 00:33:27.892
Good.
Let's get started.

00:33:27.931 --> 00:33:29.956
We will return
your entire computer system

00:33:30.033 --> 00:33:32.399
to the subterranean locale
where we found it.

00:33:32.435 --> 00:33:34.232
With the help of Mr. Kim,

00:33:34.270 --> 00:33:35.965
and a team
of Starfleet engineers,

00:33:36.039 --> 00:33:38.837
it will be an easy matter
to install the cloaking device,

00:33:38.875 --> 00:33:41.844
which will ensure your safety
for the foreseeable future.

00:33:41.878 --> 00:33:43.607
Harry, is this possible?

00:33:43.646 --> 00:33:45.238
Yes.

00:33:45.281 --> 00:33:47.078
I don't know if I believe you.

00:33:47.116 --> 00:33:48.674
I don't know yet...

00:33:48.718 --> 00:33:50.982
but I'll know soon
if you're telling the truth.

00:33:51.054 --> 00:33:52.487
You can't fool me.

00:34:01.731 --> 00:34:03.062
What does she want in return?

00:34:03.099 --> 00:34:06.034
And don't say the hostages,
because I'm not giving them up.

00:34:06.069 --> 00:34:08.537
You have to understand that
the Captain's primary concern

00:34:08.571 --> 00:34:09.936
is the safety of the hostages.

00:34:09.973 --> 00:34:12.271
She's such a warm
and noble person.

00:34:12.308 --> 00:34:15.106
I'd love her to come
to one of my parties someday.

00:34:18.948 --> 00:34:22.213
What if I promise to take
really good care of my guests?

00:34:22.252 --> 00:34:24.186
We could be more than friends.

00:34:24.220 --> 00:34:26.279
We could be... colleagues.

00:34:27.790 --> 00:34:30.122
I'm really not such a bad fella.

00:34:30.159 --> 00:34:31.592
What's happening?

00:34:31.628 --> 00:34:32.890
You tricked me!

00:34:32.929 --> 00:34:36.695
It's an attack!
It's an attack!

00:34:36.733 --> 00:34:39.099
Red Alert! Red Alert!

00:34:39.135 --> 00:34:42.468
You... you warned them.

00:34:42.505 --> 00:34:43.870
You told them
how it could be done!

00:34:44.874 --> 00:34:45.738
Take him!

00:34:52.815 --> 00:34:55.375
No, please! No!

00:35:02.392 --> 00:35:03.859
Twenty-two.

00:35:03.893 --> 00:35:05.451
More than halfway there,
B'Elanna.

00:35:05.495 --> 00:35:07.463
Captain, it's Viorsa.

00:35:07.497 --> 00:35:09.624
His norepinephrine levels
are rising sharply.

00:35:09.666 --> 00:35:11.293
No, please!

00:35:11.334 --> 00:35:15.134
I didn't do anything!
I didn't do anything!

00:35:18.608 --> 00:35:19.905
What is it?

00:35:19.942 --> 00:35:22.137
Some kind of protection device.

00:35:22.178 --> 00:35:23.509
I'm locked out.

00:35:23.546 --> 00:35:25.241
I'll have to disable it.

00:35:55.211 --> 00:35:57.475
Viorsa's norepinephrine
levels are critical.

00:35:57.513 --> 00:36:00.277
Just ten more pathways.

00:36:24.207 --> 00:36:25.174
He's dead!

00:36:25.208 --> 00:36:26.732
Massive heart failure.

00:36:30.179 --> 00:36:31.874
Captain, this one's
norepinephrine levels

00:36:31.914 --> 00:36:32.938
are approaching critical.

00:36:33.049 --> 00:36:36.576
You're next!
You're next!

00:36:38.287 --> 00:36:39.720
Restore the entire program.

00:36:42.992 --> 00:36:44.516
We've lost.

00:36:44.560 --> 00:36:47.393
We've won. We've won.

00:36:47.430 --> 00:36:48.556
We've won!

00:36:48.598 --> 00:36:51.158
Start the music.
Start the music.

00:36:51.200 --> 00:36:54.761
Celebration. Celebration.

00:36:54.804 --> 00:36:56.829
Celebration.

00:37:00.877 --> 00:37:02.276
Your decision to capitulate

00:37:02.312 --> 00:37:04.872
saved the lives
of the other hostages, Captain.

00:37:04.914 --> 00:37:07.007
You should take
some comfort from that.

00:37:07.050 --> 00:37:08.142
I don't.

00:37:10.653 --> 00:37:13.053
Have I misjudged him somehow?

00:37:13.089 --> 00:37:16.923
Is there another way
to reach him?

00:37:17.027 --> 00:37:23.364
Isn't there more to "fear"
than a simple demand to exist?

00:37:24.901 --> 00:37:28.166
Why do people enjoy
dangerous sports

00:37:28.204 --> 00:37:31.662
or holodeck adventures
with the safety off?

00:37:31.708 --> 00:37:34.575
Why, after all these centuries,

00:37:34.611 --> 00:37:37.171
do children still ride
on roller coasters?

00:37:37.213 --> 00:37:39.704
Fear can provide pleasure.

00:37:39.749 --> 00:37:41.410
To seek fear is to seek

00:37:41.451 --> 00:37:44.545
the boundaries of one's
sensory experience.

00:37:44.587 --> 00:37:47.954
But what does fear seek...

00:37:47.991 --> 00:37:52.257
at the end of the ride?

00:38:03.106 --> 00:38:04.334
You understand, don't you,
Harry,

00:38:04.374 --> 00:38:07.366
that we will have to punish you
for your Captain's little trick?

00:38:07.410 --> 00:38:08.809
To the winner go the spoils,

00:38:08.845 --> 00:38:11.245
and you are the spoils,
after all.

00:38:11.281 --> 00:38:12.578
We can talk about that later.

00:38:12.615 --> 00:38:14.640
For now, enjoy yourself.

00:38:17.620 --> 00:38:20.088
Well, you certainly know
how to bring a party to a halt.

00:38:20.123 --> 00:38:21.852
I don't get out very much.

00:38:21.891 --> 00:38:23.051
I bet.

00:38:23.093 --> 00:38:24.924
The Captain has sent me
with an ultimatum.

00:38:24.961 --> 00:38:27.930
Ultimatum?! Ultimatum.

00:38:27.997 --> 00:38:29.897
She would give me an ultimatum?

00:38:31.935 --> 00:38:34.733
Did Napoleon give an ultimatum
after Waterloo?

00:38:34.771 --> 00:38:37.501
Did Chulak of Romulus
give an ultimatum

00:38:37.540 --> 00:38:38.939
after his defeat
at Galorndon Core?

00:38:39.008 --> 00:38:42.739
We won. We give the ultimatums
around here.

00:38:42.779 --> 00:38:44.679
The Captain is prepared
to shut down the system

00:38:44.714 --> 00:38:46.875
one minute from now,
if you don't agree to her terms.

00:38:46.916 --> 00:38:49.680
And scramble the brains of all
my guests, including Harry?

00:38:49.719 --> 00:38:50.708
I don't think so.

00:38:50.753 --> 00:38:52.243
52 seconds.

00:38:52.288 --> 00:38:54.620
She is willing to risk
brain damage to the hostages,

00:38:54.657 --> 00:38:58.024
but she will end this, and end
this now, one way or another.

00:38:59.295 --> 00:39:00.319
What are her... her terms?

00:39:00.363 --> 00:39:02.126
43 seconds.

00:39:02.165 --> 00:39:04.190
She will allow you to keep
one person on the system.

00:39:04.234 --> 00:39:05.861
The other hostages
must be released.

00:39:05.902 --> 00:39:06.891
One?!

00:39:06.970 --> 00:39:08.437
Never! I won't agree.

00:39:08.471 --> 00:39:10.666
You have 30 seconds
to avoid termination.

00:39:10.707 --> 00:39:13.904
I need more time...
time to think.

00:39:13.977 --> 00:39:16.002
Two... let me keep two.

00:39:16.045 --> 00:39:17.637
20 seconds.

00:39:17.680 --> 00:39:18.738
There is another provision.

00:39:18.781 --> 00:39:20.749
The one hostage
you will be allowed to keep

00:39:20.783 --> 00:39:22.774
is Captain Janeway herself.

00:39:23.820 --> 00:39:26.380
She... would choose
to be with me?

00:39:26.422 --> 00:39:27.616
Your time is up.

00:39:27.657 --> 00:39:28.681
Your answer, please.

00:39:30.226 --> 00:39:31.659
Yes.

00:39:31.694 --> 00:39:34.162
Captain, this is the Doctor.

00:39:34.197 --> 00:39:36.188
I've returned to Sick Bay.

00:39:36.232 --> 00:39:38.826
Please turn to your emergency
medical holographic channel.

00:39:38.868 --> 00:39:40.358
Did he accept?

00:39:40.403 --> 00:39:41.563
Yes, Captain.

00:39:41.604 --> 00:39:43.299
Perfect.
Good work, Doctor.

00:39:43.339 --> 00:39:45.773
Would you like me
to return and supervise

00:39:45.808 --> 00:39:47.742
the evacuation of the hostages?

00:39:47.777 --> 00:39:49.608
I don't think that'll be
necessary, but you could

00:39:49.646 --> 00:39:51.614
help with the preparations
at this end. Janeway out.

00:39:51.648 --> 00:39:52.910
We're finished here, Captain.

00:39:52.949 --> 00:39:54.416
Initiate the recall subroutine

00:39:54.450 --> 00:39:55.940
and prepare to begin
resuscitation.

00:39:55.985 --> 00:39:57.885
Kes, give me a hand
getting hooked up to all this.

00:40:03.259 --> 00:40:04.351
Sparkling.

00:40:04.394 --> 00:40:06.828
I want everything sparkling
for her arrival.

00:40:06.863 --> 00:40:08.057
Sparkling.

00:40:08.097 --> 00:40:09.792
Uh-uh-uh-uh.

00:40:09.832 --> 00:40:11.732
Harry, not so fast.

00:40:11.768 --> 00:40:13.861
They can't have you
until I have her.

00:40:13.903 --> 00:40:14.995
No more tricks.

00:40:23.780 --> 00:40:25.873
She's coming.

00:40:25.915 --> 00:40:30.284
I can feel the system
beginning to scan her brain.

00:40:30.320 --> 00:40:31.617
Hmm... this really

00:40:31.654 --> 00:40:34.987
is such an extraordinary
gesture she's making.

00:40:35.091 --> 00:40:37.184
I am so moved.

00:40:40.463 --> 00:40:42.226
You don't quite believe it
yourself, do you?

00:40:42.265 --> 00:40:44.165
The Captain would
sacrifice herself

00:40:44.200 --> 00:40:45.360
to save the hostages.

00:40:45.401 --> 00:40:47.164
Sacrifice herself?

00:40:47.203 --> 00:40:49.865
You can be so cruel, Harry.

00:40:49.906 --> 00:40:51.897
You don't appreciate
my hospitality.

00:41:06.022 --> 00:41:07.421
You're here.

00:41:07.457 --> 00:41:09.254
You're actually here.

00:41:09.292 --> 00:41:11.157
I don't believe it.

00:41:11.194 --> 00:41:14.493
The arrangement was that
the others would be released.

00:41:14.530 --> 00:41:16.191
You show remarkable trust,
Captain.

00:41:16.232 --> 00:41:18.496
How could you be so sure
I would keep my word?

00:41:18.534 --> 00:41:20.502
I've known fear.

00:41:20.536 --> 00:41:23.334
It's a very healthy thing
most of the time.

00:41:23.373 --> 00:41:25.500
You warn us of danger,

00:41:25.541 --> 00:41:26.872
remind us of our limits,

00:41:26.909 --> 00:41:28.968
protect us from carelessness.

00:41:29.012 --> 00:41:32.140
I've learned to trust fear.

00:41:32.181 --> 00:41:36.845
Finally, someone
who appreciates me.

00:41:36.886 --> 00:41:37.853
Am I blushing?

00:41:37.887 --> 00:41:39.218
Let them go.

00:41:39.255 --> 00:41:40.950
Yes. Yes, of course.

00:41:40.990 --> 00:41:42.480
You may depart.

00:41:42.525 --> 00:41:44.356
Farewell, my friends.

00:41:44.394 --> 00:41:46.521
Do come back and visit.

00:41:46.562 --> 00:41:48.826
I'll always be here.

00:41:52.101 --> 00:41:54.126
The recall subroutine
has been activated.

00:41:54.170 --> 00:41:55.603
Body temperatures are rising.

00:41:55.638 --> 00:41:57.663
Initiating all backup systems.

00:41:57.707 --> 00:41:59.766
The hostages should
regain consciousness

00:41:59.809 --> 00:42:01.174
in less than ten minutes.

00:42:01.210 --> 00:42:03.041
We'll get you out of here,
Captain.

00:42:03.079 --> 00:42:04.341
I promise.

00:42:04.380 --> 00:42:06.439
That won't be necessary,
Mr. Kim,

00:42:06.482 --> 00:42:07.471
but thank you.

00:42:10.853 --> 00:42:13.048
I can't wait
to get to know you...

00:42:13.089 --> 00:42:14.954
to make you a part of me.

00:42:14.991 --> 00:42:17.858
As I understand it,
it takes a few minutes

00:42:17.894 --> 00:42:19.953
before you become aware
of my thoughts.

00:42:20.029 --> 00:42:21.155
Is that true?

00:42:21.197 --> 00:42:23.631
An eternity of anticipation.

00:42:23.666 --> 00:42:25.293
And then what happens?

00:42:25.335 --> 00:42:27.394
And then the fun begins.

00:42:27.437 --> 00:42:29.769
All systems functioning
as anticipated.

00:42:29.806 --> 00:42:32.366
Resuscitation
entering final warming.

00:42:32.408 --> 00:42:34.672
Bio-functions
are returning to normal.

00:42:34.711 --> 00:42:36.303
Their own hearts
are taking over.

00:42:36.346 --> 00:42:39.440
They don't need supplemental
life support any longer.

00:42:39.482 --> 00:42:41.416
Would you be honest with me?

00:42:41.451 --> 00:42:44.420
Fear is the most honest
of all emotions, Captain.

00:42:45.788 --> 00:42:49.280
You really want this to end
as much as I do, don't you?

00:42:49.325 --> 00:42:52.692
Now, now, don't even think
about leaving.

00:42:52.729 --> 00:42:55.755
I'm not going to let you go...
not after all this.

00:42:55.798 --> 00:42:57.060
Mirror?

00:42:58.134 --> 00:43:01.001
Don't we make
a beautiful couple, Captain?

00:43:01.070 --> 00:43:03.197
I'm not Captain Janeway.

00:43:04.340 --> 00:43:06.240
Could have fooled me.

00:43:06.275 --> 00:43:07.765
I'm afraid I did.

00:43:08.778 --> 00:43:09.745
Pardon?

00:43:09.779 --> 00:43:10.768
I'm nothing more

00:43:10.813 --> 00:43:12.940
than a holographic image
of Captain Janeway,

00:43:13.049 --> 00:43:17.281
sent here by the same technique
they used to send their Doctor.

00:43:17.320 --> 00:43:19.481
I've been programmed
to respond to you

00:43:19.522 --> 00:43:20.955
as Kathryn Janeway would.

00:43:21.057 --> 00:43:24.390
But... but... I-I feel you.

00:43:24.427 --> 00:43:25.689
You-you're on the system.

00:43:25.728 --> 00:43:30.131
She is on the system,
yes, but not in stasis.

00:43:31.834 --> 00:43:34.268
Captain Janeway and her
crew modified the pods,

00:43:34.303 --> 00:43:36.168
so that she could be
connected to the system

00:43:36.205 --> 00:43:38.867
without having to enter
this environment.

00:43:38.908 --> 00:43:41.342
The goal was to let you
sense her brain activity

00:43:41.377 --> 00:43:43.811
without putting her
in actual jeopardy.

00:43:43.846 --> 00:43:46.110
You will be able to confirm
what I'm telling you

00:43:46.149 --> 00:43:48.845
as soon as you become
aware of her thoughts.

00:44:07.937 --> 00:44:08.926
You know as well as I do

00:44:08.971 --> 00:44:11.838
that fear only exists
for one purpose...

00:44:11.874 --> 00:44:13.068
to be conquered.

00:44:13.109 --> 00:44:15.134
She tricked me.

00:44:15.178 --> 00:44:16.304
Did she?

00:44:16.345 --> 00:44:19.803
Or was a part of you actually
hoping to be defeated?

00:44:19.849 --> 00:44:22.943
Isn't that why you allowed
Captain Janeway to come here?

00:44:22.985 --> 00:44:26.716
Because you sensed
she had the power to subdue you?

00:44:26.756 --> 00:44:28.781
No.

00:44:28.825 --> 00:44:30.417
She lied.

00:44:30.460 --> 00:44:32.860
It was very unStarfleet of her.

00:44:32.895 --> 00:44:36.831
Starfleet Captains
don't easily succumb... to fear.

00:44:40.736 --> 00:44:43.330
What will become of us?

00:44:43.372 --> 00:44:45.863
Of me?

00:44:45.908 --> 00:44:51.369
Like all fear,
you eventually... vanish.

00:44:53.282 --> 00:44:55.147
I'm afraid.

00:44:55.184 --> 00:44:57.880
I know.

00:44:59.222 --> 00:45:00.484
Drat.
